## 5. Deterministic CLI Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

All automated Git checks report strictly **`PASS`** or **`FAIL`** (`NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`):

| Gate | Command | Pass Criterion |
|---|---|---|
| **G1 — Not on Protected Branch (`M2`)** | `git branch --show-current` | Current branch is not in `{{protected_branches}}` (`PASS`) |
| **G2 — Base Ancestry Check (`G1`, `M8`)** | `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<expected-base> HEAD` | Exit `0` (`PASS`) |
| **G3 — Staged Diff & Whitespace Hygiene** | `git diff --cached --check` | Exit `0` and only task-scoped files staged (`PASS`) |
| **G4 — Commit Message Traceability (`G3`, `M10`)** | `{{commit_check_cmd}}` | Every commit on branch cites a valid `<SUB-TICKET>`, `<PARENT-TICKET> + [PHASE-NN]`, or `(phase-NN)` (`PASS`) |
